title: Storybook1
---
<<bg 1>>
Narrator: Once there was a valley, in which flowers bloomed, and there grew a rose of a beautiful hue.
Narrator: Thunder boomed through the sky, though it stretched blue and clear. It was the soundings of war, it was the beginning of fear.
Narrator: In the men ran, violence spread through the scene. Red filled their footprints, where once there was green.
Narrator: Blossoms were scourged from their beds by their blooms. Men and roses laid down in early unearthed tombs.
<<bg 2>>
Narrator: A little rose stood alone, though it strived to survive. It grew a thistle of thorns, and it blocked out the sky.
Narrator: The war it endured, thorns gained sharpness and mass. Till at once it all ceased, there was silence at last.
Narrator: The thorns stood their guard, pointy and sheer. Though her body was frail and too dry to shed tears,
Narrator: she pinned shut her senses and just clung by a thread until fear released its grip, she would see no light shed.
Narrator: Her world, it was dim, without hope, without whim. So time passed in a haze, and her outlook stayed grim.
Narrator: The rose was shook from her trance, by a sudden advance. The ground hummed, a shadow grew, the rose trembled in her stance.
Narrator: Bracing for defense, the rose cried out in vain.
Rose: Get away, get away, or my thorns will bring you pain.
Gardener: I am a gardener. I've come to offer you my care. To tend to your ailments, to help your beauty be spared.
Narrator: "Unhand me" roared the rose.
Rose: You may not plunder me nor prune. If I never felt you near again, it would be a lifetime too soon.
Gardener: I have brought you some water; you seem awfully parched.
Narrator: Admittedly thirsty, the rose paused her remark.

-> Accept the water.
    <<jump Accept>>
-> Refuse the water.
    <<jump Refuse>>
===

title: Refuse
---
Narrator: Her thirst now awakened, she'd face sleepless nights. Her refusal of help, now the source of her blight.
Narrator: The rose remains afraid and continues to shelter. But the gardener returns, determined to help her.
<<jump Accept>>
===

title: Accept
---
Narrator: The rose flinched as he poured, though her roots expanded to hoard the sweet rain that brought end to the drought she endured.
Narrator: And no harm befell her, by the gardener's tend. But why care at all? She could not comprehend.
===
